# wget settings for the nightly recipe job, passed in as WGETRC by
# .github/workflows/nightly.yml.
#
# A job log is capped at about 2MB. wget's default dot progress writes one
# dot per KiB and fifty per line, so a line per 50KiB: mini-librispeech's
# 1.2GiB of corpus and language models comes to some 25,000 lines and
# spends the whole budget before the recipe has begun. Both attempts of
# run 45202289714 were cut off 59 bytes apart, each mid-download, leaving
# the only interesting part of the log -- what the recipe did -- unreadable.
#
# dot:giga is one dot per MiB and fifty per line, so the same 1.2GiB comes
# to about 25 lines. That keeps the transfer rate, which is worth having
# when openslr is slow enough to cost half an hour, and keeps every one of
# wget's messages.
#
# This replaces `verbose = off`, which was the first fix and threw away
# more than it had to: it suppressed the rate along with the dots. Neither
# `verbose = off` nor `quiet = on` belongs here now -- the latter would
# suppress the error messages too, which would trade one unreadable log
# for another. tests/recipes/test_nightly_logging.py forbids both.
#
# This is a setting for Kaldi's download scripts rather than a change to
# them. They are reached through the local/ symlink into the Kaldi tree
# and are not ours to edit.
progress = dot:giga
